WEBVTT

00:47.714 --> 00:48.882
Hey, mister!

00:48.965 --> 00:51.676
Have a look,
and I'll give you a good price!

00:53.011 --> 00:57.807
Believe it or not, these rugs
were woven by humans, not robots!

00:57.891 --> 00:59.517
Hey, mister!

00:59.601 --> 01:02.187
These are electronic parts
found on the battlefield!

01:02.270 --> 01:03.772
They're still usable!

01:03.855 --> 01:06.316
<i>Gesicht, that's enough. Come back!</i>

01:07.400 --> 01:11.154
<i>We'll handle all matters
related to Darius XIV's attempted suicide.</i>

01:11.654 --> 01:14.074
<i>The United States of Thracia
is too self-righteous.</i>

01:15.116 --> 01:16.910
<i>We'll confront them head-on.</i>

01:17.410 --> 01:21.039
<i>I'm fed up with that president's methods.</i>

01:21.122 --> 01:24.751
<i>Either way, we're concerned about
your physical condition.</i>

01:24.834 --> 01:27.420
<i>Professor Hoffman is worried
that your Zeronium's strength</i>

01:27.504 --> 01:30.006
<i>might have been compromised
by the cannon blast.</i>

01:30.757 --> 01:35.470
Thank you for your concern,
but I'm about to make a break in the case.

01:35.553 --> 01:37.388
<i>What? Are you sure?</i>

01:37.472 --> 01:39.682
<i>So you have an idea
of who's behind all this?</i>

01:40.308 --> 01:44.646
Yes, I think it is
what you humans would call "a hunch."

01:44.729 --> 01:47.649
<i>"A hunch"? How can a robot have a...</i>

01:48.608 --> 01:51.736
<i>Huh? Hey, Gesicht. Gesicht!</i>

01:59.536 --> 02:00.745
Are you all right?

02:00.829 --> 02:03.498
Can you stand? Here, grab onto me.

02:04.249 --> 02:05.542
Thank you, mister.

02:05.625 --> 02:08.461
Ever since I got damaged in the war,
my balance has been off.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.755
I see. Take care of yourself.

02:11.256 --> 02:13.383
Mister, please buy some flowers!

02:13.967 --> 02:17.178
Oh, I'm sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

02:17.262 --> 02:21.141
I take credit cards, you know.
Here's my reader.

02:21.766 --> 02:23.768
I'm only passing through here.

02:23.852 --> 02:26.813
I'll be leaving soon,
so I have no use for flowers. Bye now.

02:26.896 --> 02:28.356
Mister!

02:40.618 --> 02:42.328
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

02:42.412 --> 02:44.831
No, you're actually right on time.

02:45.498 --> 02:47.000
I am Gesicht of Europol.

02:47.500 --> 02:51.045
I'm Abullah, head of the Republic
of Persia's Ministry of Science.

02:58.094 --> 02:59.179
Something the matter?

03:00.054 --> 03:00.930
No.

03:03.099 --> 03:04.475
Oh, I'll have coffee.

03:05.476 --> 03:08.188
You can relax around me. I'm a scientist.

03:08.771 --> 03:11.024
They also have energy drinks here.

03:11.107 --> 03:12.984
I'm fine, sir.

03:15.778 --> 03:17.405
The look on your face tells me

03:17.488 --> 03:22.452
you're wondering if I'd prefer
an energy drink myself.

03:23.912 --> 03:27.123
Your identification system
didn't malfunction.

03:27.874 --> 03:32.003
I lost most of my body in the last war.

03:33.004 --> 03:34.339
Please excuse my rudeness.

03:34.422 --> 03:38.885
Not at all.
Thank you for coming all the way here.

03:39.510 --> 03:41.429
I wanted you to see it.

03:44.140 --> 03:48.770
<i>I wanted you to see how this country
is starting to rise from the ashes of war.</i>

03:50.104 --> 03:55.235
The nation had been reduced to rubble,
but now the bazaars are reopening.

03:57.153 --> 03:58.238
A friend of yours?

04:02.033 --> 04:02.867
No.

04:03.618 --> 04:04.661
I met him earlier.

04:05.662 --> 04:07.872
It is those children I feel pity for.

04:08.373 --> 04:10.416
Our economy is starting to recover,

04:10.500 --> 04:13.044
but the kids
in the margin of society still suffer.

04:13.753 --> 04:19.884
What we must do now
is provide them with a better life.

04:20.718 --> 04:22.220
I'm sure you understand.

04:23.763 --> 04:24.806
I do.

04:25.390 --> 04:28.017
So, what is it that you wanted to ask me?

04:28.518 --> 04:32.272
Yes, I'll get right to the point
since we don't have much time.

04:33.231 --> 04:35.817
What was your relationship
with Darius XIV?

04:38.069 --> 04:39.696
We got along fine.

04:39.779 --> 04:43.992
To his loyal subjects, he was a kind man.

04:45.118 --> 04:50.039
He often talked about turning this desert
into a country of green fields.

04:50.123 --> 04:52.583
Do you mean "fields of flowers"?

04:54.460 --> 04:55.295
Yes.

04:56.337 --> 04:58.923
Do you know a person named Goji?

04:59.924 --> 05:01.217
Can't say that I do.

05:01.301 --> 05:04.387
There's no way the head
of the Ministry of Science doesn't know.

05:04.470 --> 05:08.850
I've heard that it was a genius scientist
named Goji who enabled you to build

05:08.933 --> 05:11.769
such an advanced robot army
during Darius's reign.

05:12.312 --> 05:13.313
Only a rumor, no?

05:14.063 --> 05:17.817
That name does show up in the report
by the Bora Inquiry Commission,

05:18.318 --> 05:21.070
but his existence was never confirmed,

05:21.571 --> 05:25.992
as evidenced by the fact
that I don't know such a person.

05:26.701 --> 05:30.455
And what about the Tenma model AI
that was imported here?

05:31.331 --> 05:32.707
Tenma model.

05:33.499 --> 05:37.086
Since we're discussing rumors,
let me tell you a story that I've heard.

05:38.004 --> 05:40.423
Dr. Tenma and this genius scientist
you mentioned

05:40.506 --> 05:43.217
managed to create
the ultimate artificial intelligence.

05:43.718 --> 05:45.636
The ultimate artificial intelligence.

05:45.720 --> 05:46.554
Yes.

05:47.055 --> 05:52.435
However, said artificial intelligence
was so advanced, the robot didn't wake up.

05:52.977 --> 05:57.023
Rumors say the robot is still sleeping
somewhere in Darius's former palace.

05:58.191 --> 06:02.070
Why don't you look for
this marionette yourself?

06:04.155 --> 06:05.031
Oh dear.

06:05.114 --> 06:07.867
I'm afraid our time is up.
Please forgive me.

06:07.950 --> 06:10.119
Thank you for your time
from your busy schedule.

06:10.620 --> 06:11.996
One last question.

06:13.539 --> 06:15.291
Please take a look at this image.

06:19.337 --> 06:22.423
Have you ever seen this man before?

06:25.385 --> 06:26.719
Can't say that I have.

06:29.263 --> 06:30.139
Thank you.

06:30.973 --> 06:33.226
I appreciate your cooperation.

06:33.309 --> 06:35.144
I hope you solve the case soon.

06:35.770 --> 06:39.399
I apologize for my confusion
about whether you were a human or a robot.

06:39.482 --> 06:41.609
No, it's quite all right.

06:42.276 --> 06:44.195
I've experienced it once before

06:45.363 --> 06:47.073
when I met Atom.

06:50.034 --> 06:51.160
I see.

06:52.078 --> 06:55.456
So Atom was that advanced of a robot.

06:55.957 --> 06:56.791
Yes.

06:56.874 --> 07:00.545
But just now, my system
finally identified you as a human.

07:03.297 --> 07:04.674
Because you lied.

07:06.050 --> 07:08.678
You said you've never seen
the man in the field of flowers.

07:09.220 --> 07:12.140
My system determined that to be a lie.

07:12.807 --> 07:14.892
And robots can't lie.

07:28.781 --> 07:31.159
Mister! Please buy some flowers!

07:31.909 --> 07:33.494
You're still here?

07:33.578 --> 07:35.788
Just one is fine. Please?

07:36.330 --> 07:38.458
If you stick too long
to customers like me,

07:38.958 --> 07:40.543
your boss will get mad.

07:43.087 --> 07:44.255
Hey, mister.

07:44.839 --> 07:46.549
How about a good luck charm?

07:47.341 --> 07:52.388
Keep this on you, and it will help you
find the answers to life's problems.

07:53.264 --> 07:56.267
This is a charm of Goji,
the sage of the sands.

07:57.560 --> 07:58.603
Goji?

07:58.686 --> 08:03.107
Yes. God gave life to the sand.

08:03.733 --> 08:08.404
He's a legendary sage
who turned back to sand

08:08.905 --> 08:13.117
after showing the truth of life
to the king of the ancient Uzbek.

08:13.701 --> 08:15.077
The sage of the sands,

08:15.703 --> 08:16.537
Goji...

08:17.121 --> 08:21.792
Artificial intelligence was so advanced,
the robot didn't wake up.

08:23.836 --> 08:26.297
Just one is fine. Please?

08:28.257 --> 08:30.968
Okay, then. Just one.

08:31.052 --> 08:32.428
Thank you!

08:32.929 --> 08:34.180
What is your name?

08:34.263 --> 08:35.389
Muhammad Ali.

08:36.516 --> 08:37.767
That's a great name.

08:37.850 --> 08:40.436
Do you think I can be great like my name?

08:40.520 --> 08:42.396
Of course you can.

08:42.480 --> 08:44.815
I want to be a scholar!

08:44.899 --> 08:47.193
You can be if you study a lot.

08:47.276 --> 08:49.153
Do you think I can be like Sahad?

08:49.737 --> 08:51.030
Sahad?

08:51.113 --> 08:54.325
Yes. You showed a photo of him earlier.

08:57.370 --> 08:58.913
You mean this man?

08:58.996 --> 09:03.084
Yes! He studied abroad in the Netherlands
so he could turn this land

09:03.167 --> 09:04.752
into a field of flowers.

09:06.128 --> 09:07.255
He's my hero.

09:08.047 --> 09:10.716
You think I can be like Sahad?

09:12.635 --> 09:13.719
What's wrong?

09:14.470 --> 09:15.388
Oh, it's nothing.

09:15.888 --> 09:17.014
Sure, you can.

09:17.098 --> 09:18.432
Never lose hope.

09:19.225 --> 09:20.142
Hope?

09:20.893 --> 09:22.603
Yes, hope.

09:27.525 --> 09:28.526
Mister!

09:29.902 --> 09:31.779
Will I see you again?

09:34.615 --> 09:37.034
Yes. I'm sure we'll meet again.

09:41.122 --> 09:44.792
Yes, of course! I know Sahad very well.

09:44.875 --> 09:46.502
He used to be one of my lodgers.

09:47.003 --> 09:49.463
There, that room on the third floor.

09:49.964 --> 09:53.050
See those beautiful flowers
on the windowsills?

09:53.134 --> 09:55.845
Sahad planted all of them.

09:55.928 --> 09:57.388
They're beautiful.

09:57.471 --> 10:00.141
Oh, so even a robot like you can tell.

10:00.224 --> 10:03.269
Sahad was studying botany, right?

10:03.352 --> 10:05.187
Even after so many years,

10:05.271 --> 10:08.316
the flowers he planted
are still going strong.

10:08.899 --> 10:09.775
One time,

10:09.859 --> 10:14.196
I asked him if there were any flowers that
bloomed year-round and never withered.

10:14.280 --> 10:16.282
Those would be easy
to take care of, right?

10:16.365 --> 10:18.075
And what did he say?

10:18.576 --> 10:22.371
He said that after producing seeds,
flowers ought to wither away.

10:22.913 --> 10:24.624
He's right, I suppose.

10:28.044 --> 10:31.339
Flowers ought to wither away, huh?

10:32.506 --> 10:35.051
Ma'am, do you happen to have
a photo of him?

10:35.134 --> 10:39.764
I'm sure I have one somewhere,
but all my old data is on my old computer.

10:40.264 --> 10:42.975
It must be in storage. I'll take a look.

10:43.059 --> 10:44.435
Come by again later.

10:44.518 --> 10:45.394
Thank you.

10:45.478 --> 10:48.689
But if someone from Europol
is asking about him,

10:48.773 --> 10:50.691
should I be concerned about Sahad?

10:50.775 --> 10:52.151
No, ma'am.

10:52.234 --> 10:57.114
Of course not. Someone like him
would never get into trouble.

10:57.198 --> 10:59.492
I mean, Sahad was a truly nice person.

11:00.117 --> 11:03.329
So much so, you'd never be able to tell
he was a robot.

11:06.749 --> 11:08.918
He was an excellent student.

11:09.460 --> 11:12.838
No, excellent isn't the right word.

11:13.381 --> 11:14.382
Passionate.

11:14.965 --> 11:17.843
Yes, almost as if his life depended on it.

11:18.678 --> 11:19.762
Depended on it?

11:19.845 --> 11:24.392
Yes, because Sahad
loved his country above all else.

11:24.475 --> 11:28.979
He was devoted to filling
the Persian desert with flowers.

11:29.730 --> 11:33.025
His research was truly innovative.

11:33.109 --> 11:35.152
One day, he said to me,

11:35.236 --> 11:39.073
"Professor, look how strong
Igor has become."

11:39.156 --> 11:40.116
Igor?

11:40.825 --> 11:44.078
Or another time,
he'd say how Janus is getting sick.

11:44.161 --> 11:47.331
Or how Ishtar is getting better.

11:48.499 --> 11:50.793
They are the names of his tulips.

11:50.876 --> 11:54.964
He named all of his tulips.

11:55.047 --> 11:58.509
He said that they grew better that way.

11:58.592 --> 12:01.679
No offense, but he was a robot.

12:01.762 --> 12:05.474
The most advanced robot in Persia is made
from the best technology available.

12:05.558 --> 12:09.603
And yet, he would say
the most unscientific things.

12:09.687 --> 12:10.938
Unscientific...

12:11.522 --> 12:12.440
I see.

12:12.940 --> 12:16.235
Yes, things for which
there was no substantive basis.

12:19.280 --> 12:21.449
There's something I'd like to show you.

12:24.326 --> 12:25.161
This is it.

12:29.039 --> 12:30.249
A tulip?

12:30.332 --> 12:32.585
Sahad was growing it.

12:32.668 --> 12:35.379
And it continues to bloom
without ever withering.

12:35.463 --> 12:37.757
It never withers?
How many years has it been?

12:37.840 --> 12:39.216
Three years.

12:39.300 --> 12:43.596
He asked me not to plant it in the ground
until he got back.

12:44.346 --> 12:49.143
If he never returns,
we will end up studying this.

12:49.769 --> 12:53.647
You know, it feels as if this tulip
is waiting for him too.

12:55.024 --> 12:55.983
Oh dear.

12:56.066 --> 12:59.487
Now I've said something unscientific.

13:01.030 --> 13:02.698
Does this tulip have a name?

13:03.199 --> 13:06.702
Yes, I'm sure there must be one.

13:09.413 --> 13:11.165
Thank you for your business as always.

13:15.294 --> 13:16.128
Anton.

13:16.796 --> 13:19.089
Could you deliver this
to Mr. Van Dyke's shop?

13:19.715 --> 13:20.549
Okay!

13:22.968 --> 13:24.178
He's a hard worker.

13:24.887 --> 13:26.764
He's been a huge help.

13:28.349 --> 13:32.061
Before I came here,
I met a little flower peddler in Persia,

13:32.561 --> 13:34.730
but he wasn't working as happily as that.

13:35.523 --> 13:37.566
Persia. Sahad's country.

13:38.067 --> 13:40.361
I understand he came to this shop often?

13:40.444 --> 13:41.612
Yes, every day.

13:42.238 --> 13:45.741
He'd help me with the shop
when he had time off from school.

13:46.617 --> 13:48.828
He didn't seem to have friends.

13:49.328 --> 13:52.331
But he would talk to me
about all kinds of things.

13:53.249 --> 13:55.793
Like how he wanted to fill
his homeland with flowers.

13:56.710 --> 14:01.340
Hearing a robot like Sahad
talk about dreams made me happy.

14:02.716 --> 14:03.676
But one day,

14:04.218 --> 14:06.220
something was different about him.

14:08.681 --> 14:09.598
Out of nowhere,

14:09.682 --> 14:12.935
he told me he was going back
to his country to enlist in the army.

14:13.727 --> 14:15.980
I tried to stop him
because someone like him

14:16.063 --> 14:19.692
should never have to become a soldier,
despite how long the war raged on.

14:20.317 --> 14:21.235
And then,

14:22.611 --> 14:24.655
he told me his father died in the war.

14:25.489 --> 14:26.365
His father...

14:26.866 --> 14:28.367
I couldn't say anything.

14:29.326 --> 14:32.079
Then, with a sad look in his eye,
Sahad said,

14:33.038 --> 14:36.333
"I might end up like him."

14:37.209 --> 14:38.043
Him?

14:38.127 --> 14:41.380
What was the name of that tulip again?

14:41.463 --> 14:45.676
Yes, I heard
that he named all of his tulips.

14:46.218 --> 14:47.094
That's right.

14:47.177 --> 14:49.138
At the research site in Zaandam,

14:49.221 --> 14:54.101
he repeated many experiments to develop
a flower that could survive the desert.

14:56.145 --> 14:57.855
A stronger, more resilient flower.

14:58.480 --> 15:00.190
He wanted more and more.

15:01.233 --> 15:02.401
<i>But then, one day,</i>

15:03.152 --> 15:07.531
<i>Sahad went to the field
to check on his flowers as usual and saw...</i>

15:09.950 --> 15:11.869
<i>just one tulip standing.</i>

15:14.997 --> 15:17.041
All the flowers around it had withered.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.713
I believe the name

15:23.797 --> 15:24.673
of that flower was...

15:27.092 --> 15:28.052
Pluto.

15:36.268 --> 15:39.021
I found the photo of Sahad.

15:39.104 --> 15:41.357
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

15:41.440 --> 15:45.110
No problem. Let's see.
How do I do this again?

15:47.780 --> 15:48.656
Like so.

15:49.657 --> 15:51.241
Oh, that's right.

15:51.325 --> 15:54.495
I ask for photos
when I accept lodger applications.

15:54.578 --> 15:55.788
Ah, here it is.

15:57.623 --> 16:01.001
See? He had such a gentle smile.

16:01.085 --> 16:04.421
This photo has been cropped.

16:04.505 --> 16:05.923
Ah, yes.

16:06.423 --> 16:10.010
I think he said it was a photo
taken with his father.

16:10.094 --> 16:10.970
His father?

16:11.053 --> 16:15.391
Well, since he's a robot, he likely meant
the person who created him...

16:15.474 --> 16:16.725
This man is

16:17.768 --> 16:18.811
Professor Abullah?

16:20.562 --> 16:23.357
His father, who had supposedly died?

16:26.568 --> 16:29.405
Gesicht is getting closer.

16:30.364 --> 16:31.740
Very impressive.

16:32.241 --> 16:33.409
Don't you think so?

16:34.118 --> 16:37.746
His investigative skills are amazing,
but that's not all.

16:38.330 --> 16:41.250
His ability to fulfill missions,
the weaponry he possesses,

16:41.750 --> 16:43.335
and his Zeronium.

16:43.836 --> 16:49.717
Gesicht is the most powerful weapon
of mass destruction to date, so to speak.

16:50.592 --> 16:52.845
Pluto may lose.

16:53.387 --> 16:54.304
It's true.

16:55.305 --> 16:56.223
But you know,

16:56.890 --> 16:59.977
there is one good way to kill him.

17:00.519 --> 17:02.146
Shall I tell you?

17:03.564 --> 17:04.648
Well...

17:05.983 --> 17:08.694
From Persia to the Netherlands, huh?

17:08.777 --> 17:13.323
As I am a prisoner here,
I can't help but be jealous.

17:13.407 --> 17:18.495
But with this body,
I couldn't go anywhere even if I was free.

17:21.540 --> 17:24.209
So, you know who's behind this?

17:24.710 --> 17:25.586
Yes.

17:26.879 --> 17:28.130
Professor Abullah.

17:30.466 --> 17:32.509
<i>He was truly a great scientist.</i>

17:32.593 --> 17:35.054
<i>Dr. Ronald Newton-Howard.</i>

17:36.055 --> 17:38.474
<i>The Photon Energy he developed</i>

17:39.016 --> 17:42.895
<i>will brighten our future
like the rays of God.</i>

17:43.937 --> 17:46.440
<i>His achievements will never be forgotten...</i>

17:48.484 --> 17:50.569
You must be Epsilon.

17:54.031 --> 17:55.783
I never imagined we'd meet like this.

17:56.909 --> 17:58.494
My name is Abullah.

17:59.161 --> 18:01.580
You came all the way
from the Republic of Persia?

18:02.748 --> 18:04.458
It is truly regrettable.

18:05.334 --> 18:09.254
I wish I could have met Dr. Newton-Howard
while he was still alive.

18:10.297 --> 18:13.926
His achievements developing
Photon Energy will go down in history.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.470
As a Bora Inquiry Commission member,

18:16.553 --> 18:19.139
he helped end dictatorial rule
in the Kingdom of Persia

18:19.223 --> 18:21.141
and restored peace to the country.

18:21.225 --> 18:23.852
To lose someone like that in such a way...

18:27.606 --> 18:29.775
But then, he did leave you behind.

18:30.859 --> 18:33.487
The level of your perfection
amazes me, Epsilon.

18:34.488 --> 18:36.907
You as well, Professor Abullah.

18:37.991 --> 18:39.701
I've heard about you.

18:40.369 --> 18:43.622
How you lost most of your body
in the last war.

18:48.460 --> 18:52.464
It is nothing compared to losing family.

18:54.633 --> 18:57.511
I see. Abullah, huh?

18:58.095 --> 19:01.849
It's also just like you
to have a lack of direct evidence.

19:02.641 --> 19:06.478
But that's not all
you came here to discuss, is it?

19:07.396 --> 19:11.692
Suppose that an ultimate
artificial intelligence exists.

19:12.484 --> 19:16.822
If a robot were equipped with
an artificial intelligence too advanced,

19:17.406 --> 19:18.657
what would happen?

19:20.409 --> 19:22.119
It wouldn't wake up.

19:22.202 --> 19:23.370
And why is that?

19:23.453 --> 19:27.124
Because it would not know what to become.

19:27.207 --> 19:30.794
In order to simulate all
9.9 billion personalities on the planet,

19:30.878 --> 19:33.338
it would take an eternity.

19:33.422 --> 19:35.299
As such, it wouldn't wake up.

19:36.133 --> 19:38.010
Then how could it be woken up?

19:40.846 --> 19:44.975
By introducing extreme emotions to it.

19:46.185 --> 19:48.937
Extreme emotions?

19:51.106 --> 19:52.274
Hatred.

19:52.357 --> 19:53.734
That's right.

19:55.235 --> 19:56.195
Anger.

19:56.278 --> 19:57.446
Yes.

19:58.322 --> 19:59.156
Sorrow.

19:59.239 --> 20:00.532
Correct!

20:00.616 --> 20:02.868
Then, it would wake up.

20:05.287 --> 20:06.622
Now,

20:06.705 --> 20:10.834
what kind of robot
would it turn out to be when it awakened?

20:16.632 --> 20:18.508
It looks like it's about to rain.

20:19.468 --> 20:22.179
Your powers weaken
on a day like this, don't they?

20:22.679 --> 20:23.513
Yes.

20:23.597 --> 20:26.975
Well, you have no need
for such mighty powers anyway.

20:27.601 --> 20:30.270
You refused to participate in that war,

20:31.063 --> 20:32.564
and you were right to do so.

20:33.106 --> 20:35.025
There is no such thing as a just war.

20:37.069 --> 20:39.404
You lost your family in the war.

20:40.155 --> 20:44.201
My wife, my children...
The war took everything from me.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.210
Tears.

20:58.507 --> 20:59.758
The rain has started.

21:00.425 --> 21:02.177
And it appears the funeral is over.

21:02.678 --> 21:03.637
Yes.

21:06.348 --> 21:07.391
Epsilon.

21:08.308 --> 21:10.852
What is most important to you?

21:20.070 --> 21:24.032
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting!
The funeral is over, so let's go home!

21:24.116 --> 21:25.284
Okay, Epsilon!

21:25.367 --> 21:26.493
Epsilon!

21:26.576 --> 21:27.911
We saw a squirrel over there!

21:27.995 --> 21:29.746
- Really?
- I found an acorn!

21:29.830 --> 21:31.123
You can have it, Epsilon!

21:31.748 --> 21:32.749
How wonderful.

21:33.333 --> 21:36.169
I had heard that you adopted war orphans.

21:39.673 --> 21:41.758
Please take good care of these children.

21:42.551 --> 21:47.222
Love these children,
for me and the ones that I've lost.

21:51.101 --> 21:54.146
I must attend
the European Robotics Conference.

21:55.272 --> 22:00.277
The restoration of Persia requires that
we create more wonderful robots like you.

22:08.243 --> 22:10.954
Hey, I don't see Wassily.

22:11.038 --> 22:11.872
Yeah!

22:13.165 --> 22:14.333
Wassily!

22:14.416 --> 22:16.835
- Wassily, where are you?
- Wassily!

22:16.918 --> 22:17.794
Oh!

22:18.628 --> 22:19.504
There he is!

22:20.130 --> 22:22.215
Wassily, we're going home.

22:25.260 --> 22:26.511
What's wrong, Wassily?

22:27.888 --> 22:28.805
Bora.

22:31.266 --> 22:32.309
Bora.

22:33.935 --> 22:34.853
It's all right.

22:35.354 --> 22:37.689
This is not a battlefield.
Don't be scared.

22:40.650 --> 22:41.860
Bora.

22:43.195 --> 22:44.571
It will lie.

22:45.864 --> 22:48.700
Once this robot gained consciousness,
it would tell lies.

22:49.326 --> 22:52.454
To others, of course, but also to itself.

22:54.289 --> 22:57.167
You are close to solving this case.

22:57.959 --> 23:00.670
Where is Pluto now?

23:00.754 --> 23:04.549
He must be undergoing maintenance
to tend to the damage he received

23:04.633 --> 23:06.134
in the fight with Hercules.

23:06.843 --> 23:08.178
He's probably back home.

23:08.678 --> 23:09.513
Home?

23:10.305 --> 23:12.182
Sahad's homeland, Persia?

23:12.682 --> 23:15.560
No, Pluto's home.

23:18.105 --> 23:20.232
The tulip.

23:25.612 --> 23:27.280
<i>Abullah's whereabouts?</i>

23:27.364 --> 23:30.492
Yes, we must take him
into custody right away.

23:30.575 --> 23:32.702
<i>Don't be ridiculous, Gesicht!</i>

23:32.786 --> 23:33.954
<i>He's a VIP!</i>

23:34.037 --> 23:37.249
It doesn't matter!
I need to know where he is!

23:37.332 --> 23:39.668
<i>And what do you intend to do?</i>

23:40.710 --> 23:42.587
I will go to where Pluto is.

23:42.671 --> 23:44.756
<i>Pluto? Where he is?</i>

23:44.840 --> 23:48.301
The Kingdom of Persia has an agricultural
research facility in the Netherlands.

23:48.802 --> 23:51.430
It's in Zaandam,
on the outskirts of Amsterdam!

24:09.698 --> 24:11.658
<i>Just one tulip standing...</i>

24:12.951 --> 24:14.828
All the flowers around it had withered...

24:15.787 --> 24:17.414
The name of that flower was

24:18.206 --> 24:19.207
<i>Pluto.</i>

24:20.417 --> 24:21.251
It's close.

24:23.003 --> 24:23.879
Pluto...

24:28.675 --> 24:31.386
<i>What a fantastic speech!</i>

24:31.887 --> 24:36.266
You absolutely deserved
that standing ovation, Professor Hoffman.

24:36.349 --> 24:38.393
Thank you very much.

24:39.102 --> 24:41.897
Despite the hardships
you've faced recently,

24:41.980 --> 24:45.859
we truly appreciate you attending
the European Robotics Conference.

24:46.651 --> 24:49.404
Did you find
the security we provided satisfactory?

24:49.488 --> 24:53.325
Yes. Thanks to them,
I was able to carry out an important duty.

24:54.034 --> 24:57.037
Professor Hoffman,
your helicopter is here.

24:58.079 --> 25:02.000
As you can see, these brawny bodyguards
are giving me door-to-door service.

25:02.584 --> 25:05.003
I'll go check the heliport.

25:05.086 --> 25:08.215
No, I'm sure they have
their own security there.

25:08.298 --> 25:10.926
Still, you can never be too careful.

25:11.009 --> 25:14.763
Professor Hoffman, the entire world
of robotic engineering depends on you.

25:16.014 --> 25:18.016
Thank you. Goodbye.

25:18.099 --> 25:18.975
Please, take care.

25:20.977 --> 25:22.812
Uh, I need to use the bathroom.

25:22.896 --> 25:23.980
I've checked it.

25:24.064 --> 25:26.233
Then I will be fine on my own.

25:42.541 --> 25:45.919
Well, that was a wonderful speech.

25:47.963 --> 25:51.716
I was especially moved by your remarks
about the potential for Zeronium

25:51.800 --> 25:53.552
to contribute to peace.

25:54.219 --> 25:55.095
And you are...

25:55.845 --> 25:58.181
It's a pleasure to meet you,
Professor Hoffman.

25:58.765 --> 26:01.184
I'm Abullah from the Republic of Persia.

26:15.240 --> 26:17.617
Just a regular power generator
in the basement.

26:21.997 --> 26:24.040
<i>They're faint,
but these electromagnetic waves</i>

26:24.124 --> 26:27.669
<i>are the same as those recorded by Epsilon
during the fight with Hercules.</i>

26:28.503 --> 26:29.462
<i>It's close.</i>

26:39.264 --> 26:40.473
You!

26:42.767 --> 26:45.604
I've always wanted to speak with you.

26:45.687 --> 26:49.232
After all, you're the one
who brought Gesicht into this world.

26:49.316 --> 26:50.400
The pleasure is mine.

26:50.483 --> 26:53.862
If there's anything I can do
to help with the restoration of Persia...

26:53.945 --> 26:56.114
Zeronium is the perfect metal.

26:56.197 --> 26:59.576
Perhaps you could consider
deregulation of Zeronium imports.

26:59.659 --> 27:00.660
Right...

27:01.494 --> 27:06.082
Even the culprit who's going around
destroying the most advanced robots

27:06.166 --> 27:07.834
wouldn't win against Gesicht.

27:08.418 --> 27:09.711
I suppose not.

27:09.794 --> 27:11.671
I heard a rumor

27:11.755 --> 27:14.716
that Gesicht was recently damaged
by a cluster cannon.

27:14.799 --> 27:19.137
Oh, yes, you're very well-informed.
But please do not worry.

27:19.220 --> 27:20.805
It wasn't serious.

27:20.889 --> 27:22.891
Wonderful.

27:22.974 --> 27:25.310
Even damage to that degree
will not affect him?

27:25.393 --> 27:26.269
Yes.

27:26.353 --> 27:27.771
I see.

27:27.854 --> 27:30.732
Then, Gesicht has no weaknesses.

27:30.815 --> 27:33.234
No, he does have flaws.

27:33.318 --> 27:35.445
It's just that layers and layers

27:35.528 --> 27:37.614
of advanced control systems
are built into him.

27:38.573 --> 27:41.326
I see. So you're saying
that prevents error?

27:41.409 --> 27:42.786
Error?

27:42.869 --> 27:46.790
Well, he doubts and struggles,
just like we do.

27:47.374 --> 27:49.751
Is that what you meant by "flaws"?

27:49.834 --> 27:52.712
Those systems are the source
of his strengths and flaws.

27:52.796 --> 27:57.926
Given his superiority, what would you do
if he were to make an irreparable mistake?

27:58.510 --> 27:59.844
For example...

28:01.888 --> 28:03.973
if he killed someone.

28:22.283 --> 28:23.201
You lot!

28:24.994 --> 28:26.496
What are you protecting?

28:27.539 --> 28:29.916
A robot that kills humans.

28:30.583 --> 28:33.378
There was such a robot once,
was there not?

28:34.170 --> 28:35.797
Brau1589.

28:36.339 --> 28:40.176
Apparently, he described what he did
as an "execution."

28:40.927 --> 28:44.347
The same logic humans use
when they commit murder.

28:45.432 --> 28:46.850
What are you trying to say?

28:47.434 --> 28:51.312
Well, is that not
what the world did to Persia

28:51.396 --> 28:55.525
after you and other Bora Inquiry
Commission members entered the nation?

28:57.819 --> 29:00.029
Please forgive me. I've gone too far.

29:00.697 --> 29:04.117
After all, democracy has taken root
in Persia, thanks to you.

29:06.453 --> 29:09.664
But if a robot did happen to kill a human,

29:10.415 --> 29:13.376
I think that robot should be executed.

29:15.879 --> 29:19.215
If Gesicht ever did such a thing,

29:20.091 --> 29:21.718
what would you do?

29:21.801 --> 29:23.595
That would never happen!

29:24.220 --> 29:28.308
A robot as advanced as Gesicht
could even take his own life.

29:28.892 --> 29:30.935
- Nonsense!
- No.

29:31.019 --> 29:34.731
Perhaps the authorities would erase such
memories from Gesicht before he did so.

29:37.233 --> 29:40.278
Did you do something to him?
His artificial intelligence--

29:40.361 --> 29:43.782
All you need to do
is to maintain him properly.

29:44.407 --> 29:45.325
Director!

29:46.326 --> 29:47.994
What did you do to Gesicht?

29:50.330 --> 29:52.874
Robots' memories can be deleted.

29:53.374 --> 29:55.084
I can't help but envy them.

29:56.961 --> 29:58.880
I wish I could do the same.

30:02.425 --> 30:05.178
<i>Gesicht, this is Europol Headquarters.
Can you hear me?</i>

30:05.261 --> 30:06.846
Yes, I can.

30:06.930 --> 30:09.766
<i>We've located Abullah. He's in Düsseldorf.</i>

30:09.849 --> 30:11.976
<i>He's attending
the European Robotics Conference.</i>

30:12.060 --> 30:14.646
Understood. Take him into custody
as soon as possible.

30:14.729 --> 30:18.942
<i>The thing is, Professor Hoffman
is also attending that conference.</i>

30:19.025 --> 30:19.859
What?

30:19.943 --> 30:21.611
Professor Hoffman?

30:22.237 --> 30:23.613
Thank you for waiting.

30:23.696 --> 30:25.114
Let us get going, sir.

30:32.288 --> 30:33.540
Is everything okay, sir?

30:34.916 --> 30:36.876
Oh, no, I'm fine.

30:38.127 --> 30:39.212
It is the same thing.

30:41.214 --> 30:42.257
The same thing.

30:43.007 --> 30:45.134
What the world did to Persia.

30:45.718 --> 30:47.053
They must be executed.

30:54.102 --> 30:56.396
Please confirm Professor Hoffman's safety.

30:56.479 --> 30:57.772
I'll be there soon--

31:16.457 --> 31:17.709
This is Europol!

31:17.792 --> 31:19.627
This building is now on lockdown!

31:19.711 --> 31:21.713
What? What's going on?

31:21.796 --> 31:23.339
Nobody goes in or out!

31:23.423 --> 31:26.759
Stay where you are
until instructed otherwise!

31:26.843 --> 31:30.555
Excuse me! Please take a look
at the elevator monitor!

31:35.018 --> 31:36.102
Professor Hoffman!

31:36.686 --> 31:40.398
The elevator is heading toward
the heliport on the top floor.

31:40.481 --> 31:42.692
Damn it! Get up there now!

31:42.775 --> 31:45.111
None of the other elevators are working!

31:45.194 --> 31:46.279
What?

31:46.779 --> 31:49.407
What the hell is that thing?

31:51.367 --> 31:55.038
Aren't you supposed to be
my robot bodyguard?

31:55.121 --> 31:59.375
Did something else
hijack your artificial intelligence?

31:59.459 --> 32:02.879
<i>Professor Hoffman, can you hear me?
Please stay calm, and don't--</i>

32:06.674 --> 32:09.385
Are you the one who killed
all those scientists?

32:10.762 --> 32:13.097
You must be executed.

32:15.183 --> 32:17.477
Gesicht. Can you hear me, Gesicht?

32:18.144 --> 32:20.772
<i>Professor Hoffman
has been abducted. Gesicht!</i>

32:20.855 --> 32:23.441
I can hear you.
I'm headed there as soon as I can.

32:24.525 --> 32:25.902
However, right now,

32:26.986 --> 32:29.489
right in front of me is...

32:36.579 --> 32:41.584
Is this because of
what the commission did in Persia?

32:42.168 --> 32:46.714
I do feel responsible.
But what would killing me achieve?

32:49.092 --> 32:51.219
Open up! Open the door!

32:52.220 --> 32:55.974
That's your partner.
He's on your side too, isn't he?

32:56.057 --> 32:57.392
I'm opening the door now!

32:58.810 --> 33:00.853
Professor, run!

33:12.699 --> 33:13.825
Horns.

33:14.450 --> 33:19.664
That's how you're going to kill me too?
Just what are you?

33:19.747 --> 33:22.250
Bora...

33:23.251 --> 33:24.085
What?

33:25.795 --> 33:28.548
Bora...

33:30.299 --> 33:32.427
Squad A here.
We're almost at the heliport!

33:34.053 --> 33:36.347
What the hell is with these cockroaches?

33:42.228 --> 33:46.107
Target sighted. He has captured
Professor Hoffman and is on the move.

33:46.983 --> 33:49.068
We do not have a clear shot as it stands.

33:50.445 --> 33:52.030
<i>- Do it anyway.</i>
- What?

33:52.113 --> 33:53.990
It's fine. Take the shot!

33:55.241 --> 33:59.412
But what about Professor Hoffman's safety?

34:07.879 --> 34:11.424
What about the professor?
Is Professor Hoffman safe?

34:14.677 --> 34:17.513
My body is made of Zeronium.

34:18.014 --> 34:20.308
Thermal and magnetic rays
won't work on me!

34:23.853 --> 34:25.980
If you move, I'll shoot!

34:26.064 --> 34:27.106
Freeze!

34:38.951 --> 34:42.622
Its combat capabilities plummeted
from 1,200,000 to 5,800.

34:45.500 --> 34:47.126
It buried itself alive, huh?

34:47.710 --> 34:50.630
This is Gesicht!
I have captured the target.

34:51.130 --> 34:52.757
Is Professor Hoffman safe?

34:55.051 --> 34:57.386
What do you want us to do, Captain Becker?

35:00.473 --> 35:01.599
Yes, he's fine.

35:02.475 --> 35:04.018
<i>Destroy the target.</i>

35:19.992 --> 35:23.746
Illusions like this won't work
on my artificial intelligence!

35:25.289 --> 35:26.707
A field of flowers...

35:26.791 --> 35:28.209
- Pluto...
- Huh?

35:29.669 --> 35:31.254
Pluto...

35:34.132 --> 35:35.925
- Pluto!
- No!

35:36.425 --> 35:37.844
You are not Pluto!

35:38.469 --> 35:43.474
Pluto!

35:43.558 --> 35:46.018
Your name is Sahad!

36:01.951 --> 36:05.496
Yes. You are Sahad.

36:07.039 --> 36:07.874
Sahad.

36:09.208 --> 36:10.042
Sahad.

36:16.465 --> 36:17.758
Father.

36:18.718 --> 36:20.970
You're alive, Father.

36:21.053 --> 36:22.305
I'm so glad.

36:22.805 --> 36:26.350
I received news that you were
also killed in the airstrike.

36:27.101 --> 36:27.935
Thank God.

36:28.019 --> 36:29.103
Yes.

36:29.937 --> 36:31.898
But I've lost everything.

36:32.982 --> 36:35.359
As a robot, I'm sure
that you understand this.

36:35.443 --> 36:37.904
I've lost most of my body.

36:38.571 --> 36:40.114
But more importantly,

36:40.198 --> 36:43.993
my wife, Fatima, my daughter, Lola,

36:44.577 --> 36:47.205
and your robot brother, Murat.

36:48.247 --> 36:49.624
Those barbarians.

36:50.541 --> 36:54.045
They took the family I held precious!

36:54.128 --> 36:56.923
My most beloved treasure!

36:58.174 --> 36:59.091
Father...

37:00.635 --> 37:01.928
Now, all I have is you.

37:03.095 --> 37:07.225
You are all I have left, Sahad!

37:07.725 --> 37:09.268
You understand, don't you?

37:09.769 --> 37:11.103
How I feel.

37:13.898 --> 37:15.274
Hatred.

37:18.569 --> 37:20.154
I have a favor to ask of you.

37:21.405 --> 37:23.241
Please save this country.

37:25.409 --> 37:28.621
Do not let them kill
any more of our people.

37:29.413 --> 37:35.002
Do not let our people
experience sorrow like I have.

37:38.047 --> 37:39.465
We must take revenge.

37:40.549 --> 37:42.677
This war will soon be over.

37:43.177 --> 37:45.346
Revenge only begets more revenge.

37:45.972 --> 37:48.641
The hatred would never fade away!

37:48.724 --> 37:49.600
That's right.

37:50.851 --> 37:53.521
Hatred never fades.

37:59.318 --> 38:02.613
Let me install your brain
into the strongest of bodies.

38:04.532 --> 38:06.450
The strongest of bodies?

38:11.163 --> 38:12.540
What is this, Father?

38:15.001 --> 38:18.879
I love you, Sahad.

38:20.256 --> 38:21.340
Father...

38:23.092 --> 38:25.094
I love you.

38:32.727 --> 38:33.602
<i>Gesicht!</i>

38:34.228 --> 38:36.188
<i>What are you doing? Shoot it now!</i>

38:36.272 --> 38:37.648
I give my authorization!

38:38.232 --> 38:39.275
<i>Destroy the target!</i>

38:44.530 --> 38:45.740
<i>No.</i>

38:47.158 --> 38:48.159
What did you say?

38:48.242 --> 38:52.872
I am not programmed to destroy a robot
that has no intention of attacking.

38:53.622 --> 38:54.540
What the...

38:55.082 --> 38:56.334
Gesicht, listen to me.

38:56.834 --> 38:59.378
You destroy that thing,
and the case is solved.

38:59.462 --> 39:00.338
This is an order.

39:00.421 --> 39:01.380
<i>Take the shot!</i>

39:01.464 --> 39:02.298
I refuse.

39:02.381 --> 39:05.509
Gesicht! How could you say that?

39:05.593 --> 39:06.761
In the past, you've...

39:09.513 --> 39:12.725
Listen, Gesicht.
I'm ordering you once again.

39:13.517 --> 39:15.394
<i>Destroy the target at once, and--</i>

39:15.478 --> 39:16.687
I said no. That's final.

39:17.271 --> 39:18.356
<i>Gesicht!</i>

39:23.736 --> 39:24.737
<i>Captain Becker,</i>

39:25.363 --> 39:27.656
<i>do I have the right to resign?</i>

39:27.740 --> 39:28.574
Huh?

39:29.325 --> 39:30.951
<i>Stop with the nonsense.</i>

39:31.035 --> 39:35.122
<i>You were developed as a robot detective.
You do not have a choice!</i>

39:35.664 --> 39:38.751
Then I'd like to request
a leave of absence for one year.

39:38.834 --> 39:39.919
<i>You what?</i>

39:40.586 --> 39:42.546
I've had enough.

39:47.385 --> 39:48.219
Right?

39:52.014 --> 39:53.974
<i>Is Professor Hoffman safe?</i>

39:54.975 --> 39:56.435
<i>He is safe.</i>

39:56.519 --> 39:57.353
That's a lie.

39:58.896 --> 40:03.025
I just accessed the camera
of the Science Forum's heliport.

40:03.109 --> 40:05.361
<i>What is that robot?</i>

40:05.861 --> 40:08.322
<i>The robot that has Professor Hoffman.</i>

40:08.406 --> 40:10.282
It's...

40:10.366 --> 40:11.200
<i>Captain Becker.</i>

40:11.951 --> 40:18.457
You ordered me to fire even though
Professor Hoffman was in such danger.

40:20.835 --> 40:21.961
<i>Gesicht.</i>

40:23.504 --> 40:24.964
<i>Let's make a deal.</i>

40:25.464 --> 40:26.298
Who are you?

40:26.882 --> 40:28.759
<i>Let's exchange hostages.</i>

40:29.343 --> 40:31.971
<i>Release my beloved Pluto.</i>

40:32.471 --> 40:33.556
Who are you?

40:34.306 --> 40:39.603
<i>Step away from there,
and I will release Professor Hoffman.</i>

40:42.982 --> 40:43.816
<i>Gesicht!</i>

40:44.400 --> 40:46.026
Do not act without permission!

40:51.782 --> 40:52.950
Gesicht!

40:54.243 --> 40:55.953
<i>Your actions are in violation of</i>

40:56.036 --> 41:00.958
<i>Article 1, Clause 3 and Article 15,
Clause 2 of the Robot Laws,</i>

41:01.041 --> 41:02.710
<i>and you will be penalized severely!</i>

41:02.793 --> 41:03.627
<i>Gesicht!</i>

41:07.381 --> 41:09.049
This is from the heliport.

41:09.133 --> 41:12.595
The robot that had Professor Hoffman
suddenly collapsed!

41:14.388 --> 41:15.681
I've secured the professor!

41:29.195 --> 41:30.029
Sahad.

41:33.282 --> 41:36.702
Your father does not love you.

41:45.044 --> 41:46.212
Are you crying?

42:02.394 --> 42:03.687
Oh, Gesicht.

42:04.188 --> 42:06.398
<i>Hey, Helena. You're still working?</i>

42:06.899 --> 42:07.733
Yes.

42:07.816 --> 42:09.527
But I'm ready for a break soon.

42:10.069 --> 42:11.487
- How about you?
<i>- Right.</i>

42:14.114 --> 42:14.949
<i>It's finished.</i>

42:15.032 --> 42:16.408
Really?

42:16.492 --> 42:18.619
<i>Yes. Really.</i>

42:18.702 --> 42:23.082
You say that now, but I know you'll be
on your next assignment in no time.

42:23.165 --> 42:24.333
<i>This time is different.</i>

42:24.917 --> 42:27.294
<i>Let's take that trip to Japan
for real this time.</i>

42:28.045 --> 42:30.172
<i>From now on, I will have plenty of time.</i>

42:31.382 --> 42:35.261
You sound as if you're going to quit
being a detective.

42:38.973 --> 42:41.308
<i>Shall we apply
for permission to adopt a child?</i>

42:45.688 --> 42:47.147
We've tried before.

42:47.731 --> 42:51.652
<i>Yes, but we couldn't find
a good match for us back then.</i>

42:52.152 --> 42:53.654
<i>Things are different now.</i>

42:54.196 --> 42:57.866
<i>Robotics has advanced,
and the regulations have been relaxed.</i>

42:59.785 --> 43:01.870
I wonder if I'll make a good mother.

43:02.413 --> 43:03.706
<i>Of course you will.</i>

43:04.290 --> 43:05.332
<i>I know it.</i>

43:06.041 --> 43:07.876
- What?
<i>- Um, well...</i>

43:08.961 --> 43:12.631
<i>Besides, if we had children,
you wouldn't feel lonely.</i>

43:12.715 --> 43:14.216
I'm not lonely.

43:15.342 --> 43:16.677
I have you.

43:18.679 --> 43:21.140
<i>We'll talk more when I get home.</i>

43:21.223 --> 43:23.350
Okay. Come home soon.

43:23.976 --> 43:24.810
<i>I will.</i>

43:34.653 --> 43:37.323
<i>Professor Hoffman, are you all right?</i>

43:37.406 --> 43:40.576
Yes, I'm all right, Gesicht.

43:41.118 --> 43:43.245
I'm more worried about you.

43:43.329 --> 43:44.663
<i>I'm not injured.</i>

43:44.747 --> 43:47.333
And the monster?
I was told you cornered it.

43:47.416 --> 43:50.544
<i>Yes, it's only a matter of time
until it gets captured.</i>

43:50.628 --> 43:54.214
Good. There's no need for you
to confront it face-to-face again.

43:54.298 --> 43:56.258
Your body is not in optimum condition.

43:56.342 --> 43:57.176
<i>Yes.</i>

43:57.259 --> 43:59.303
Anyhow, now we know who's behind it.

43:59.386 --> 44:01.764
- Just as you said...
<i>- Abullah.</i>

44:02.348 --> 44:06.226
Yes, the robot bodyguard
that attacked me was hijacked by him.

44:06.310 --> 44:08.354
It was all Abullah's doing.

44:08.437 --> 44:10.773
<i>What bothers me is
Professor Ochanomizu's statement.</i>

44:10.856 --> 44:12.900
<i>He said the true culprit is Dr. Goji.</i>

44:13.400 --> 44:15.653
Goji and Abullah, huh?

44:16.195 --> 44:19.740
For now, leave things to the others.
You must rest.

44:19.823 --> 44:21.700
I hate to repeat myself,

44:21.784 --> 44:25.454
but because of that cluster cannon blast,
your Zeronium body has metal fatigue.

44:25.537 --> 44:27.956
If you experience
another shock like that, then--

44:28.040 --> 44:28.999
<i>Professor Hoffman.</i>

44:30.542 --> 44:33.295
<i>About the dreams
I've been telling you about...</i>

44:33.379 --> 44:34.254
Yes?

44:34.338 --> 44:38.008
<i>I may not have them anymore.</i>

44:38.092 --> 44:39.426
What do you mean?

44:40.427 --> 44:43.430
<i>I'm not sure. I just have a feeling</i>

44:44.056 --> 44:47.434
<i>that I've figured out
the true nature of my dreams.</i>

44:47.518 --> 44:51.021
What? Wait, does that mean
your memory has...

44:51.522 --> 44:52.815
<i>Until next time, Professor.</i>

44:52.898 --> 44:54.650
Wait, Gesicht!

45:02.241 --> 45:04.576
<i>Zaandam Agricultural
Research Facility to base.</i>

45:04.660 --> 45:05.869
<i>Squad D has arrived.</i>

45:05.953 --> 45:07.538
<i>We're heading underground.</i>

45:08.664 --> 45:11.166
<i>Squad F here,
currently doing a search underground.</i>

45:11.250 --> 45:14.503
<i>We're almost at the spot where
Detective Gesicht cornered the target.</i>

45:16.046 --> 45:19.216
<i>The target's combat capabilities
have declined significantly,</i>

45:19.299 --> 45:20.342
<i>but keep your guard up.</i>

45:20.426 --> 45:21.427
<i>Destroy it on sight!</i>

45:22.094 --> 45:24.179
I repeat! Destroy it on sight!

45:25.097 --> 45:26.557
- Director.
- Where's Gesicht?

45:26.640 --> 45:28.809
He's on his way to Amsterdam.

45:28.892 --> 45:31.854
I heard the report.
Contact Gesicht immediately!

45:31.937 --> 45:34.732
Yes, sir. As soon as
things are ready at Zaandam--

45:34.815 --> 45:35.816
Do it right now!

45:38.360 --> 45:41.238
<i>Gesicht, why are you acting on your own
without permission?</i>

45:41.321 --> 45:45.200
Not only are you disobeying orders,
you say you want to resign?

45:45.284 --> 45:48.996
<i>And if you can't resign,
you want an extended leave of absence?</i>

45:49.079 --> 45:50.372
<i>I will not allow either!</i>

45:50.456 --> 45:53.125
<i>Your artificial intelligence
is malfunctioning.</i>

45:53.208 --> 45:57.629
<i>You must undergo maintenance right away
and then report to the advisory committee.</i>

45:58.297 --> 45:59.715
<i>Are you listening, Gesicht?</i>

45:59.798 --> 46:03.177
There's something that must be done
before any of that, isn't there?

46:04.595 --> 46:06.638
Why didn't you punish me?

46:10.684 --> 46:14.563
<i>I committed a crime
deserving of execution.</i>

46:15.272 --> 46:17.149
Why did you erase my memory?

46:19.234 --> 46:20.736
My precious...

46:26.700 --> 46:28.619
Don't you dare cut out, Gesicht!

46:28.702 --> 46:30.329
<i>Gesicht!</i>

46:38.962 --> 46:42.424
You're such a hard worker, Anton,
working so late.

46:42.925 --> 46:45.803
Yes! I'll be done after this delivery.

46:46.345 --> 46:47.596
Hello, Gesicht.

46:47.679 --> 46:50.057
Hello. I'd like
a bouquet of flowers, please.

46:50.140 --> 46:52.226
Of course. Who is it for?

46:52.309 --> 46:53.560
For my wife.

46:53.644 --> 46:55.521
How nice. I'm jealous.

46:56.396 --> 46:58.440
What kind of flowers would she like?

46:59.983 --> 47:01.652
He's alive, you know.

47:03.487 --> 47:05.030
Sahad is alive.

47:06.782 --> 47:07.658
Is it true?

47:08.325 --> 47:10.452
Did he do something wrong?

47:12.371 --> 47:13.664
He didn't do anything bad.

47:14.998 --> 47:16.124
It's not his fault.

47:44.570 --> 47:45.612
Hello, Anton.

47:45.696 --> 47:46.697
We meet again.

47:55.539 --> 47:56.373
You are

47:56.957 --> 47:59.167
Ali from the bazaar in Persia.

48:01.295 --> 48:03.714
Why are you in Amsterdam?

48:12.055 --> 48:13.682
You can have the whole body for 500 ZEUS.

48:18.020 --> 48:19.229
He walked.

48:19.730 --> 48:21.732
He walked, Gesicht.

48:31.742 --> 48:32.618
You're...

48:43.420 --> 48:46.006
Ali, come here.

48:46.089 --> 48:47.716
No need to be scared.

48:48.216 --> 48:51.470
You heard the gunshot, right?
It's dangerous here.

48:51.553 --> 48:53.263
Come this way.

48:56.934 --> 48:59.728
You know, I have a little one like you.

49:02.814 --> 49:03.649
Ali!

49:04.316 --> 49:05.692
What's wrong, Ali?

49:51.655 --> 49:56.702
<i>Last night, in Amsterdam's Old Town,
a robot agent was murdered.</i>

49:57.536 --> 50:01.707
<i>The victim was one of the most
advanced robots in the world, Gesicht.</i>

50:01.790 --> 50:04.418
<i>A deactivated small D-class robot</i>

50:04.501 --> 50:07.045
<i>with a cluster cannon on its arm
collapsed nearby.</i>

50:08.380 --> 50:13.010
<i>Detective Gesicht suffered damage
from the same weapon a few weeks ago,</i>

50:13.093 --> 50:16.972
<i>and he was involved in an intense battle
hours before his death.</i>

50:17.806 --> 50:19.141
<i>His strongest...</i>

50:34.281 --> 50:37.909
Welcome. It's been a long time,
Professor Hoffman.

50:37.993 --> 50:41.621
Since the inquiry commission,
Professor Ochanomizu.

50:41.705 --> 50:43.165
Allow me to introduce you.

50:43.248 --> 50:45.834
I'm Helena, Gesicht's wife.

50:49.212 --> 50:52.758
I don't know what to say.
I'm truly sorry for your loss.

50:53.467 --> 50:55.594
If there's anything I can do to help...

50:55.677 --> 50:59.639
Oh, I'm truly grateful
that you invited me here.

51:00.265 --> 51:04.770
Gesicht was looking forward
to visiting Japan again together.

51:05.437 --> 51:08.815
In fact, he made reservations
for the trip on the day he died--

51:08.899 --> 51:12.486
Minister Ochanomizu, we should get going
before the media finds us.

51:13.028 --> 51:13.904
Ah, yes.

51:15.822 --> 51:18.492
She's put on a brave face.

51:19.034 --> 51:23.080
You think Gesicht is another victim
of the series of robot destruction?

51:23.163 --> 51:26.708
Yes, though Europol refuses
to reach a conclusion just yet.

51:27.834 --> 51:30.921
Our lives may still be in danger as well...

51:31.004 --> 51:32.172
Professor Ochanomizu?

51:32.672 --> 51:34.966
It's just as Gesicht said.

51:35.050 --> 51:35.967
What is?

51:36.635 --> 51:41.932
He told me that the air in Japan
has a faint trace of soy sauce.

51:45.727 --> 51:49.106
KAMINARIMON

52:07.916 --> 52:11.419
She's trying to act like
she's enjoying herself in order to forget.

52:11.503 --> 52:14.005
That is
some extremely sophisticated behavior.

52:14.673 --> 52:15.507
Indeed.

52:16.216 --> 52:20.887
Even though robot memories are permanent
unless you erase them from their AI...

52:21.471 --> 52:26.184
It seems that Europol tampered
with Gesicht's memory.

52:26.810 --> 52:27.811
"Tampered"?

52:28.311 --> 52:30.605
Was it within the standards
of the Robot Laws?

52:30.689 --> 52:32.858
No, as an extrajudicial measure.

52:33.483 --> 52:34.734
That's not good.

52:34.818 --> 52:38.405
I looked into it,
but I couldn't get to the truth.

52:38.989 --> 52:43.160
It's wrong for humans to tamper
with robot memories as they please.

52:44.703 --> 52:46.288
But now, I want...

52:50.125 --> 52:51.293
to erase them for her.

52:52.460 --> 52:54.296
I actually asked her

52:54.379 --> 52:57.007
if she wanted to erase
any parts of her memory.

52:57.674 --> 53:00.468
Then she said to me,

53:01.970 --> 53:04.764
"Please don't erase my memories of him."

53:18.904 --> 53:21.573
Mr. Hoffman, your room is the Maple Room.

53:22.282 --> 53:24.659
Miss Helena, your room is the Pine Room.

53:25.619 --> 53:28.288
This is the room Gesicht booked for us.

53:28.955 --> 53:30.582
Will you be okay alone?

53:31.625 --> 53:34.211
- Yes.
- Right this way, ma'am.

53:44.638 --> 53:46.640
I can find my own way from here.

53:47.140 --> 53:48.308
Very well, ma'am.

53:57.984 --> 53:59.444
You must be Dr. Tenma.

54:00.195 --> 54:01.238
I am.

54:01.321 --> 54:02.405
Do you have it?

54:07.953 --> 54:11.122
Will this help find the culprit?

54:11.206 --> 54:12.666
Of course.

54:15.835 --> 54:16.795
Dr. Tenma.

54:19.339 --> 54:20.590
What's the matter?

54:21.383 --> 54:23.760
I can't process it all.

54:24.427 --> 54:25.262
Process what?

54:25.762 --> 54:28.556
The overwhelming amount of grief.

54:29.516 --> 54:34.020
Memories of Gesicht
just get clearer and clearer.

54:35.105 --> 54:37.732
I don't know what to do.

54:38.775 --> 54:41.361
Helena, go ahead and cry.

54:43.613 --> 54:46.741
When things like this happen, humans cry.

54:50.161 --> 54:50.996
Yes.

54:52.414 --> 54:54.541
You can start by imitating.

54:58.461 --> 54:59.504
That's right.

55:09.597 --> 55:10.974
Very good.

55:11.057 --> 55:12.559
You're doing great.

55:13.810 --> 55:17.230
It may be an imitation,
but eventually, it becomes the real thing

55:18.231 --> 55:19.607
like it did for me.

55:20.483 --> 55:22.861
You'll be able to truly cry.

55:24.779 --> 55:25.655
These are

55:27.282 --> 55:28.992
real tears.

55:32.996 --> 55:34.372
Atom is dead,

55:36.082 --> 55:37.834
and I am heartbroken too.

58:18.411 --> 58:22.081
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
